             stead of _s_t_d_i_n.  Since it lacks user interaction, it should be
             used in conjunction with non-interactive authentication to obvi‐
             ate the need to enter a password at connection time (see sshd(8)
             and ssh-keygen(1) for details).

             A _b_a_t_c_h_f_i_l_e of ‘-’ may be used to indicate standard input.  ssffttpp
             will abort if any of the following commands fail: ggeett, ppuutt,
